# --- Secrets & credentials (never commit) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# --- Logs & temporary files ---
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
*.bak
*~
*.orig

# --- OS / IDE ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Python runtime junk ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- Junk files from the stuck-VS-Code-terminal artifact (see AGENTS.md hand-over):
# --- if these reappear in the repo root, they are not real project files.
/noop
/arg_value
/setsid
/sleep

# --- Raw game data & player submissions (transient — convert first, keep the
# --- TSV result, never commit the raw upload). Whether an uploaded test/data
# --- file should be kept depends on what kind it is, so the defaults are:
#
# WDB client caches from Cache/WDB (convert with tools/parse-wdb.py):
*.wdb
# /wps fel reports from players (SavedVariables dump):
WPSDB*.lua
# Collector SavedVariables dumps:
VarldenAvKrigskraft_Collector.lua
WPSCollectorDB.lua
*CollectorDB*.lua

# --- NOTE on test files ---
# Proper offline unit tests (tests/test_*.py) ARE committed - the whole agent
# pipeline depends on them (`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` must end OK).
# Uploaded/ad-hoc test data of the kinds above (*.wdb, WPSDB*.lua, *Collector*.lua)
# is NOT committed regardless of which session produced it. A one-off test file
# that does not match those globs must be judged by hand: commit it only if
# another developer needs it to reproduce a result.

# --- Local notes and agent config ---
saker_som_behover_fixas.md
att_gora.txt
found_issues/
.clinerules
.cline*
